<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila Central Bank sets trend for weaker peso.</title>
<headline>Manila Central Bank sets trend for weaker peso.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>--------------------------- Oct 3 --------------------------</p>
<p>* Power firm's $18 million demand also pulls down peso</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The Central Bank set the pace for a weaker peso on Thursday when it raised its offer rate for the dollar to 26.28 from 26.26, traders said.</p>
<p>The peso closed at 26.26 pesos to the dollar from 26.246. The day's average was at 26.257 versus 26.245, with turnover rising to $114 million from $102.20 million.</p>
<p>&quot;The Central Bank pushed up the dollar,&quot; a local bank trader said.</p>
